==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
Formed from the numeral {{m|is|tíu}}, perhaps by directly reanalizing the ''-u'' as the weak feminine oblique suffix in environments where ''tíu'' is the object in a sentence. Compare {{m|is|nía}} and {{m|is|átta}}, also {{m|is|fimma}}, {{m|is|sexa}}, {{m|is|sjöa}}.

